From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Opaniuk <igor.opaniuk@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:12:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] net: qrtr: ns: keep going when an announcement cannot be
 sent

announce_servers() answers a HELLO by announcing every local server to
the new node, and stops at the first send error: the node then never
learns about the servers after that one. ctrl_cmd_new_server() returns
before lookup_notify() when the broadcast of a new local server fails,
so lookups already registered for that service, including the ones of
remote nodes, are never told the server exists.

A send failure to one node says nothing about the others. Log it and
carry on in both places.

Fixes: 0c2204a4ad71 ("net: qrtr: Migrate nameservice to kernel from userspace")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Igor Opaniuk <igor.opaniuk@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/linux-arm-msm/patch/14899597/

[ from patchwork.kernel.org series 1188830 (patch 14899597, 1 of 2); not applied upstream yet;
  carried in denialwm/linux-perpetua 9b73b0d47b22. Patch 2 of 2 (hold control packets behind
  the HELLO gate) is not picked: our queue covers that window with ca4ac2d8a714, 8bb6cc355630
  and 73d520a4bd36 ]
[ upstream author: Igor Opaniuk <igor.opaniuk@oss.qualcomm.com>; picked for the iceland kernel q90y ]
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/qrtr/ns.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/qrtr/ns.c b/net/qrtr/ns.c
index 33a9c4449d6f..09b25107f760 100644
--- a/net/qrtr/ns.c
+++ b/net/qrtr/ns.c
@@ -239,7 +239,7 @@ static int announce_servers(struct sockaddr_qrtr *sq)
 				continue;
 
 			pr_err("failed to announce new service\n");
-			return ret;
+			/* the remote needs the other servers no less */
 		}
 	}
 	return 0;
@@ -495,10 +495,12 @@ static int ctrl_cmd_new_server(struct sockaddr_qrtr *from,
 
 	if (srv->node == qrtr_ns.local_node) {
 		ret = service_announce_new(&qrtr_ns.bcast_sq, srv);
-		if (ret < 0) {
+		/*
+		 * A failed broadcast must not hide the server from the
+		 * lookups already registered for it.
+		 */
+		if (ret < 0)
 			pr_err("failed to announce new service\n");
-			return ret;
-		}
 	}
 
 	/* Notify any potential lookups about the new server */
